  "notes": "Cash basis, governmental funds only (no business-type funds). Statement lines from the Governmental Funds Total column (p4); fund balance 15,308,096 + receipts 10,665,457 - disbursements 11,147,936 + transfers in 2,995,934 - out 2,995,934 = 14,825,617. Beginning cash not printed (no prior-year balance column); ending_cash = printed Cash and cash equivalents 10,004,572 (restricted cash 1,066,768 and investments 3,754,277 separate). Statement Taxes 5,699,365 split by fund name only for the Inheritance Tax Fund (483,007) and Visitors Promotion fund (35,238, lodging); the remainder 5,181,120 has no printed tax-type breakdown. On p4 and p10 the Other Nonmajor values print slightly offset from their row labels; rows assigned so the Total column ties (Veterans Aid 1 = Intergovernmental – Other; Preservation 5,144 and Juvenile Diversion 2,931 = Charges for Services; Federal Drug 7,816 = Miscellaneous). Statement of Activities Miscellaneous 293,421 = fund statement Miscellaneous 293,396 + Licenses and Permits 25. Detail: General Fund budget schedule (p5, departments with no object breakdown, zero-actual lines Juvenile Center and Public Health – Program Supplies omitted); major fund budget schedules (p6-p8), with Road & Bridge and COVID one-line DISBURSEMENTS split by the fund's p4 column (budget_final in split_from); nonmajor funds from the nonmajor combining statement (p10) rather than the one-line nonmajor budget schedule (p9) to avoid double counting. Balance sheet from the governmental funds statement of cash basis assets and fund balances (p3; totals equal the Statement of Net Position p1). Read pages 1-10 of 10"
